# Shore spec

Read `00-beacon-shared.mdc`, then `docs/TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` §8, §9, §10, §11 (Shore/Both tables), §13, §16. Payloads: `beacon_contract.sync` (sync routes) and `beacon_contract.shore_api` (dashboard routes).

## 1. Stack
FastAPI (Python 3.12) on **Cloud Run** `shore-api`, region **asia-southeast1** · **Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector** (asyncpg via the Cloud SQL Unix socket) · SQLAlchemy 2 async + Alembic · **Cloud Storage** bucket `byf-beacon-2026-media` (private, signed URLs 10 min) · ffmpeg/ffprobe + Pillow in the image · `google-genai` (Vertex AI) through `shore/app/ai/gateway.py` (Sumit) · JWT auth (pyjwt + argon2).
DECISION: the built dashboard (`web/apps/dashboard/dist`) is served by shore-api at `/` (same origin, no CORS, one deploy). API at `/api/v1`.

## 2. GCP setup (Phase 0: start Cloud SQL first, it takes 10–15 min)
```
gcloud config set project byf-beacon-2026
gcloud services enable run.googleapis.com sqladmin.googleapis.com aiplatform.googleapis.com \
  storage.googleapis.com cloudbuild.googleapis.com artifactregistry.googleapis.com secretmanager.googleapis.com
gcloud sql instances create beacon-pg --database-version=POSTGRES_16 --edition=ENTERPRISE \
  --tier=db-custom-1-3840 --region=asia-southeast1 --storage-size=10GB
gcloud sql databases create beacon --instance=beacon-pg
gcloud sql users create beacon --instance=beacon-pg --password='<strong>'
# then: CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;   (first Alembic migration does this)
gcloud storage buckets create gs://byf-beacon-2026-media --location=asia-southeast1 --uniform-bucket-level-access
gcloud iam service-accounts create shore-api
# roles: cloudsql.client, aiplatform.user, storage.objectAdmin (bucket), iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator (self, signed URLs)
gcloud run deploy shore-api --source . --region asia-southeast1 --service-account shore-api@byf-beacon-2026.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
  --add-cloudsql-instances byf-beacon-2026:asia-southeast1:beacon-pg --allow-unauthenticated \
  --no-cpu-throttling --min-instances 1 --memory 1Gi \
  --set-env-vars SHORE_DB_SOCKET=/cloudsql/byf-beacon-2026:asia-southeast1:beacon-pg,SHORE_AI=vertex
```
Local dev: Postgres in Docker (`pgvector/pgvector:pg16`, port 5434) and `SHORE_AI=fake`. Build context must include `contract/` and `web/apps/dashboard/dist` (deploy from the repo root with a `shore/Dockerfile`, or copy them in a `make build` step; document whichever you pick).

## 3. Data (§11 Shore + Both tables)
`vessels, shore_users, tickets, ticket_media, ticket_actions, ticket_messages, ai_analyses, accident_corpus, learnings, learning_media, learning_targets, learning_stats, checkin_aggregates, anchor_cards, anchor_stats, sync_state` plus:
- `processed_events(event_id PK, vessel_id, applied_at)` (idempotency)
- `pull_changes(seq bigserial, change_id, vessel_id, type, payload jsonb, created_at)`; cursor = `seq` as a string
- `audit_log(id, actor, action, ticket_id/learning_id, at)` for accept, reject, reply, publish, retract
- `tickets` never has `reporter_crew_id`; `embedding vector(768)`; `accident_corpus.embedding vector(768)`
Seed (`make seed`): `seed/vessels.json` (each with an API key printed once; store sha256), shore users `reviewer@byf.demo` / `admin@byf.demo` (demo passwords in `.env.example`), `seed/shore_tickets.json` (backdate `received_at`), `seed/accident_corpus.jsonl` (embed on load).

## 4. Sync routes (`/api/v1`; vessel key + HMAC via `beacon_contract.security.verify_request`; reject > 5 min skew)
| Route | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `GET /healthz` | Link probe, no auth, fast |
| `POST /sync/push` | `SyncDelta` (gzip body) → `PushResponse`. Per event: if `event_id` processed → `duplicate`; else apply by **field ownership** (ignore any shore-owned field from the edge), insert `processed_events`, ack `applied`. A bad event → `rejected` with error; others still apply. New ticket → `shore_status=NEW`, enqueue the AI analysis job (background task: embeddings, similar tickets, corpus match, Gemini analysis). |
| `GET /sync/pull?cursor=&limit=200` | `PullResponse` of `pull_changes` for this vessel with `seq > cursor` |
| `POST /sync/media/{ticket_media_id}` | photo upload (only after its ticket exists); strip EXIF; to GCS |
| `GET /sync/media-url/{learning_media_id}` | `LearningMediaUrl` (signed, 10 min), only for learnings targeted at this vessel |

Every shore-side change a ship must see (shore_status, shore messages, learning published/retracted, fleet alert, brief enrichment, anchor scheduled, rail update) inserts a `pull_changes` row built from the matching `beacon_contract.sync` change model.

## 5. Dashboard routes (§13.2; JWT; roles `shore_reviewer`, `shore_admin`)
`POST /auth/login` (`ShoreLogin` → `ShoreToken`) · `GET /tickets` (filters incl. `updated_since`, default sort severity desc then age → `list[ShoreTicketListItem]`) · `GET /tickets/{id}` (`ShoreTicketDetail`, signed photo URLs) · `GET/POST /tickets/{id}/analysis` (`AiAnalysis`) · `POST /tickets/{id}/accept` (NEW → IN_REVIEW, `assigned_to`) · `POST /tickets/{id}/reject` (`RejectRequest`) · `POST /tickets/{id}/close` (`CloseRequest`) · `GET/POST /tickets/{id}/messages` (sender `shore`; resolve to `reporter_ref`, enqueue `ticket_message`) · `GET /tickets/{id}/similar` · `POST /learnings/draft` (`LearningDraftRequest` → `LearningDraftLLMOutput`) · `POST /learnings`, `PATCH /learnings/{id}` (`LearningPatch`), `POST /learnings/{id}/media`, `POST /learnings/{id}/publish`, `POST /learnings/{id}/retract`, `GET /learnings` (`LearningListItem`) · `GET /fleet/overview` (`FleetOverview`, wellbeing tiles only when n ≥ 5) · `GET /fleet/clusters` (`HazardCluster`) · `GET/POST /anchor/cards`, `POST /anchor/draft-week`, `PATCH /anchor/cards/{id}`, `POST /anchor/cards/{id}/approve|retract` · `GET /vessels`.
Every status change, reply, publish and retract writes `audit_log` and the matching `pull_changes`.

## 6. Learning media (§10.1)
- Image (JPEG/PNG/WebP) → resize 1280 px → WebP.
- GIF → looping muted MP4 (P2).
- Video: `ffprobe` duration ≤ 6.0 s else 422 with the measured duration; re-encode H.264 480p, no audio, target < 1.5 MB.
- Total media per learning ≤ 2 MB. Store sha256 and bytes (sent in `LearningMediaManifest`).
- Publish: write `learning_targets` per vessel (`same_vessel` → the ticket's vessel; `selected_vessels`; `all_vessels`) and a `learning.published` pull change per vessel. Urgent learnings set `priority=urgent`.

## 7. Similarity and clusters
- Similar tickets: pgvector cosine on `tickets.embedding`, other vessels first, last 90 days, top 5 with score.
- Corpus: top 3 on `accident_corpus.embedding`.
- Clusters (P1): connected components of tickets with cosine ≥ 0.85 in the last 30 days spanning ≥ 2 vessels; label with Gemini. HDBSCAN is P2.

